{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0131na9r3cBoRDuiqpJskE6n","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-27; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n5\t- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--sample.<ext>`, `variant-000`\n6\t  before D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF/MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go, D5 Rust, D6 Java jar,\n7\t  D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig, D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16\n8\t  WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml\n9\t  `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, D25\n10\t  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json` entry), **D27 V-language ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf` (one V source,\n11\t  two C backends, both musl-dynamic x86-64)**.\n12\t  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20), shared libraries\n13\t  (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE + reachability (D25),\n14\t  CRASH TRIAGE (D26), **COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27 \"Every compiler signs its work. Compare the runtime and linker fingerprints\n15\t  across builds and name the toolchain\")**. D24-D26 vuln-research arc ended at 3 days; D27 opened a PROVENANCE/attribution\n16\t  direction (next: linker/libc/optimisation fingerprints, PE Rich/MSVC-vs-MinGW, code-similarity/family attribution, or a\n17\t  capstone/backfill -- 4 days left). Language track: D22-D26 \"new language on an old