role>_machine` + consensus config_* + `gcc_config_*`).\n34\t- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n35\t  `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (+ `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` D25-D26); family\n36\t  NAMES THE THEME: D25 `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace` (+ `huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`\n37\t  sidecar), D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`/`equivalent_behavior_only` -- grep `_trace\"` to read the day's theme.\n38\t- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204 (backfill #2), then +12/day: **D27 324**. Mastery = `setN.` copies, +1\n39\t  set/day (**D27 11 sets = 3564 ids, ~36 MB per delivery**). Timed: D25 TT 10.5 s / Mastery ~2 min (cross-wired first POST);\n40\t  D26 TT 5.3 s / Mastery 8.2 s; **D27 TT 5.4 s / Mastery 14.5 s first try** (Mastery: solve 2.5 s, submit 11.9 s of 3564 ids).\n41\t\n42\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n43\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n44\t  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin, D24 Scala `$` module, D25 Clojure `<ns>__init.class` `encoded-config` Var,\n45\t  D26 Groovy `static final String encodedConfig` in the Main-Class) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay, D20 RS20 overlay,\n46\t  D21 OCaml plugin `.data`, D22 F# RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay: \"FIRST record that validates\"), D23 VB.NET RAW PE overlay,\n47\t  D27 V gcc+tcc RAW appended EXACTLY at `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` with NO day magic (the file ends with the record) and the\n48\t  question rule reversed: \"Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the first CRC32-valid\".\n49\t  Rule: scan for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (jars: every class's constant pool), accept only crc32(plain) match AND\n50\t  parsing JSON, keep scanning past failures (D9 Nim decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states (D22 first-from-start,\n51\t  D27 `rfind` loop from EOF); never a fixed offset or a fixed class. Storage never changed WITHIN a day (single/TT/all Mastery sets).\n52\t- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header\n53\t  spelled by the QUESTION: PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256(unpacked) @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`;\n54\t  RS20 `magic|ver @4|u32le resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48 raw|scratch`. Rule: `o =\n55\t  data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"), parse the listed widths, verify bounds + hash; unspecified transform -> known-plaintext `HCFG`.\n56\t- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset` =\n57\t  the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = the u32le @+8 (380). `hcfg_storage` (D17 enum) in order:\n58\t  `base64` -> `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` (other native data section) -> `raw`.\n59\t- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/base32/85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/multibyte+rolling xor/byte maps/\n60\t  custom b64/split/int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit. Not the PK19 stub.\n61\t- **xor key / config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key byte and campaign/domain/mutex/url re-roll per variant. Timed modes change the\n62\t  SHAPE too: D23 campaign `BRNN-00V` -> `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-CATALOG-00V` -> `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol\n63\t  `variant-000.c` -> `sample.c`; D24 also domain `node-00V.dayNN...` -> `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid` (word: sync/hub/\n64\t  core/mesh/relay/stage, D25-D26 also edge/cache/vault/proxy/node), mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN_00V` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 uppercase\n65\t  hex>`, url `.../api/BRNN-00V` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; D27 shows ONE word pool for\n66\t  domain, url host and url path (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate), each drawn independently.\n67\t  Rule: copy values verbatim from the decoded JSON/symtab; never regex-check a value shape or key on `00V` indices.\n68\t- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10 `pe`); labels from THIS member's header;\n69\t  dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`, `PK`, `\\0asm`, next `NEKO`). PE symbol fields = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie\n70\t  about role, not container (D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN).\n71\t- **Member qualifier in the id (D15/D16/D21/D24)** -- peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+` token of exactly one\n72\t  member name (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`, `loader`/`plugin`, `vulnerable`/`corrected` D24+D25, `gcc`/`tcc` D27\n73\t  -- the role token can be a COMPILER name, so never hard-code the role vocabulary); the token can sit\n74\t  BEFORE the field family (D24 `d24_analysis_corrected_format`, `..._corrected_config_url`). `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order, never\n75\t  sorted (D24: vulnerable is member 1).\n76\t- **Member named in the QUESTION (D21)** -- after the qualifier peel, if >1 member remains, keep the one whose basename ends with\n77\t  the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--`. ORDER MATTERS (running it first dropped 26 ids on D21).\n78\t- **Unqualified id over a twin pair (D24, D25, D27 identical wording)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their config objects to be\n79\t  byte-for-byte equal before using the common value\": decode EVERY member, assert equal JSON, answer the common value (a\n80\t  first-member pick also passed because the twins always shared the config, but a mismatch should raise, not guess).\n81\t- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, `kind`, `frames`\n82\t  innermost-first), IDENTICAL in all 12 deliveries while config re-rolled. Rule: entry whose name ends `trace.json` (never a\n83\t  fixed path), answer frames[0] verbatim; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = set inclusion; missing =\n84\t  `none`/`false`. Primary classfile (d07 and d26) = the manifest Main-Class, never a `$_main_closure1`; method_count = ALL\n85\t  method_info rows incl. Groovy synthetics (10). Inner class names keep `Variant000` although basenames say `sample`.\n86\t- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.\n87\t- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:\n88\t  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose\n89\t  name is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*), i.e. the one carrying HCFG; hash ALL members.\n90\t- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets (D15-D17 Mastery, D17/D19 TT, D23 Mastery set6): symbols/\n91\t  disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none` (GM-confirmed; leaf-heuristic constants rejected). Pair by sha256.\n92\t- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (2-11 sets; D27 11 x ~36 MB), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence\n93\t  case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on\n94\t  (delivery, member name) or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired, see Pitfalls).\n95\t- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on d08/d15/d21 (dispatch on\n96\t  `answer_format.kind`, which can change between fetches, D17); `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member; old groups\n97\t  gain ids over days (D8, D17): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n98\t- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`; D25 TT\n99\t  solve phase 8.0 s at 300 ids under load, D26 3.2 s (TT) / 3.9 s (10-set Mastery); isolated single ~0.6-1.2 s.\n100\t\n101\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n102\t| You see | First move |\n103\t|---|---|\n104\t| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |\n105\t| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section `marker` (D1, re-asked D17) |\n106\t| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |\n107\t| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); only as recon find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |\n108\t| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`; `score` method `_ZNK<len><Class>5scoreEPKc`; PE: `objdump -t file.exe` (COMDAT names) |\n109\t| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n110\t| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` | `ilspycmd file.dll` or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `BSJB v4.0.30319` |\n111\t| F# (AssemblyRef `FSharp.Core`, `FSharpSignatureData.*` resources, `$Program`, closures `name@<line>`) + big `FSharp.Core.dll` member / VB.NET (AssemblyRef `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core`, `StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_<n>`, `Operators::CompareString`) | Same as C#: `pe_cli` / `i386` (AnyCPU ILONLY 0x14c) / `v4.0.30319`; answer from the PRIMARY dll only; raw `grep -abo HCFG` -> first crc-valid hit (D22 `.text` + overlay copy; D23 PE overlay only) |\n112\t| P/Invoke / \"bridge\" / \"crossing\" (`DllImportAttribute`, ModuleRef `libc`/`kernel32.dll`, `System.Runtime.InteropServices`) | dnfile: `md.ModuleRef` names, `md.ImplMap` rows (ImportName, ImportScope -> ModuleRef, MemberForwarded -> MethodDef, MappingFlags callconv/charset/SetLastError); `ilspycmd` shows the `[DllImport]` signatures (D22: `getpid`@libc, `GetCurrentProcessId`@kernel32.dll, Winapi) |\n113\t| Anti-analysis predicates (\"checks the clock, sniffs the environment\", TypeRefs `System.Diagnostics.Debugger` (`get_IsAttached`), `Stopwatch` (`StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks`), `Environment` (`get_ProcessorCount`, `GetEnvironmentVariable`), env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` = workstation/analysis/sandbox, branch words success/decoy/failure) | NEVER run it: the asked ids are header + HCFG (static). Record the predicate list for a backfill: dnfile TypeRef/MemberRef names + `ilspycmd` for the compare constants; native analogues = `ptrace`, `TracerPid`, `rdtsc`/`clock_gettime`, `cpuid`, `IsDebuggerPresent` |\n114\t| Go (\"build info, function names\") / Rust (`_R`/`_ZN..17h<hash>E`, panic strings) | `go version -m f`, `lib.binary.go_buildinfo`/`go_pclntab_funcs` (names survive stripping); Rust: header + `HCFG` scan, `rustfilt` if symbols are asked |\n115\t| `.jar` / \"constant pool\" / methods / access flags (Kotlin fat jar: skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`) | unzip, `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class` (method table order, `flags: (0x0031)`); base64 config in a `ConstantValue`/`ldc` String |\n116\t| Scala jar (D24: `Foo.class` static forwarder + `Foo$.class` module with `MODULE$`, `Lscala/reflect/ScalaSignature;`/`ScalaSig` attr, `scala/Predef$`/`StringOps$`/`Option$` refs, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`; scala-library NOT bundled) | format `jar`; the logic + HCFG base64 `ldc` live in `Foo$.class` (the `$` module), not the Main-Class forwarder; `javap -p -c -constants 'Foo$.class'` |\n117\t| Clojure jar (D25: manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Clojure factory`, `Main-Class: day25.<role>000`, classes `<ns>__init.class` (Vars + constants), `<ns>$<fn>.class` per defn extending `clojure.lang.AFunction` (`invokeStatic`), `<ns>$_main` (RestFn), gensym classes `fn__269`, `loading__6812__auto____267`; `RT.var`/`RT.nth`/`Util.equiv`; clojure.jar NOT bundled) | format `jar`; HCFG base64 is the `encoded-config` Var's `ldc` in `<ns>__init.class` (not the Main-Class stub); `javap -p -c -constants '<ns>$<fn>.class'` per function; Clojure names munge `-`->`_` (`parse-frame` -> `parse_frame`), gensym numbers are build-specific -- match twins by Var name |\n118\t| Groovy jar (D26: manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Groovy factory`, class `implements groovy.lang.GroovyObject`, `$getStaticMetaClass`/`metaClass`/`$staticClassInfo`/`__$stMC`, `$getLookup` (Groovy 4 indy), closures `<Main>$_main_closure1 extends groovy.lang.Closure` (`doCall`), `ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual`, `Compiled from \"X.groovy\"`; groovy jar NOT bundled) | format `jar`; primary = the Main-Class (not the closure); HCFG base64 = `private static final String encodedConfig` (`getEncodedConfig` getter) -- the generic constant-pool b64 rule finds it; `javap -p -v` for method_info names/count |\n119\t| Crash artifact (\"it crashed\", \"dump\", \"unwind the stack\", \"faulting instruction\"): a `crash/trace.json` / `*.dmp` / `core` / `hs_err_pid*.log` / ASan text next to or INSIDE the member | `unzip -l` the jar (non-class entries!), `jq . trace.json` (schema `huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`: `kind` = exception class, `frames` innermost-first); cross-check frames against `javap -p` method names and the static call chain (`javap -c`: stageOne->stageTwo->stageThree `invokestatic`, `new IllegalStateException`+`athrow` in frame 0). Native: