mat enum lists `neko_bytecode` since D19) | Neko VM bytecode (Haxe/nekoc): `neko`/`haxe` are apt-installable; globals table holds the string constants -> HCFG scan; format `neko_bytecode` |\n129\t| `kind: enum` + `accepted_values` + \"Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order\", or text describing bytes (\"Read k1 at +5 ... ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1 ... verify the SHA-256\") | The question IS the spec (D17, D19): implement it literally over the parsed facts, emit one listed token; don't reverse the stub first |\n130\t| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!`; or a real code-reversing question | `lib.binary.packer_info` -> `upx -d` on a COPY (UPX unseen); `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless `lib.binary.ghidra_decompile` (last resort) |\n131\t\n132\t## Day by day\n133\t**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (~14 min, 4 wrong): C ELF64 headers, `.huntress`, recover_code. **D2 \"Mangled\"** (~22 min): C++ ELF/MinGW PE,\n134\tfirst HCFG; PE symbols = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. **D3 \"Table Manners\"** (~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong): .NET, format `pe_cli` after ~50\n135\tsynonyms. **D4 \"Go Fish\"** (1.5 min): `amd64` REJECTED → `x86-64`. **D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (7 s). **D6 \"Pool Party\"** (~5 min): jar\n136\tconstant-pool base64 HCFG. **D7 \"Routine Check\"** (3 min): Kotlin fat jar. **D8 \"Swift Justice\"**: 67 MB Swift; backfill #1 to 10\n137\tids/group; integer elf_class/machine. **D9 \"Nimble\"** (86 s): raw decoys, NEW `hcfg_offset`. **D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (33 s): NEW\n138\t`has_hcfg_section`. **D11 \"D-Day\"** (36 s). **D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (54 s): HCFG RAW. **D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (14 s). **D14\n139\t\"Selective Memory\"** (9 s): ObjC, `.hcfg`. **D15 \"Stripped\"** (74 s): stripped/symbolized pair, `<qualifier>_` ids. **D16 \"Wasm\n140\tUp\"** (91 s): compact/direct wasm pair, `wasm`/`wasm32` first try via the prebuilt `wasm_layout`.\n141\t**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"** (204 Qs): Ada; backfill #2; `hcfg_storage` burned ~10.9k POSTs / 3.5 h until revised to an enum.\n142\t**D18 \"Flow State\"** (T+11 s): Fortran, call-graph theme unasked. **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"** (T+2:25): GnuCOBOL + `PK19` packed\n143\toverlay; NEW `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`; the questions spelled the stub. **D20 \"Resourceful\"** (T+49 s): Haskell + `RS20`\n144\toverlay; NEW `hcfg_resource_size`. **D21 \"Shared Custody\"** (T+1:33): OCaml loader + `.cmxs` plugin; question-named member\n145\trouting AFTER the qualifier peel (running it first dropped 26 ids).\n146\t\n147\t**D22 \"Bridge Troll\"** (T+47 s): F# `sample.dll` + runtimeconfig + 5.7 MB `FSharp.Core.dll` support member; P/Invoke theme\n148\tunasked; HCFG RAW twice (\"FIRST record that validates\"); basenames renamed `variant-000` -> `sample`. **D23 \"Trust Issues\"**\n149\t(T+84 s): VB.NET, HCFG RAW only as PE overlay; anti-analysis predicates unasked; timed modes re-shaped values. **D24 \"Spot the\n150\tDifference\"** (T+35 s): Scala twin jars `-vulnerable`/`-corrected` (only `score(String)I` changed, CWE-476); 12 ids = 2 sha256 +\n151\t`<role>_format` + 4 consensus config_* + 4 `corrected_config_*`; HCFG `ldc` in the `Foo$` module. **D25 \"Out of Bounds\"** (T+80 s,\n152\tzero new code): Clojure AOT twins, `parse-frame` unguarded `(nth frame 4)` (CWE-125) gated by `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT`; same 12-id\n153\ttemplate; Mastery 9 sets first POST cross-wired 55 ids (`id(bytes)` caches) -> CORRECT ~2 min via localize + live worker.\n154\t\n155\t**D26 \"Crash Course\"** (312 Qs; CORRECT T+76 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.3 s / Mastery 10 sets 8.2 s): one Groovy 4 jar (Main-Class\n156\t`Day26Variant000`, static stageOne->stageTwo->stageThree, stageThree throws IllegalStateException) + a `crash/trace.json` sidecar\n157\t(`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, frames innermost-first). Theme ASKED: `crash_fault_method` = frames[0], `crash_frames_match_methods`\n158\t= frames subset of the Main-Class method_info names (`true`); `method_count` 10 (d07 \"Day 26\" leak). Race solver banked 310 ids at\n159\tT+45 s; ~15 lines for the sidecar