{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017icMDvgyQ7r7kDqtGqkV1u","type":"tool_result","content":"d02_analysis_vtable_symbol {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"first exact matching symbol name in the specified table traversal; preserve section prefixes and mangling; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d02-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Determine the d02 member format from final-byte magic. For ELF64, traverse only SHT_SYMTAB sections in section-header order and their entries in entry order. For PE, traverse primary COFF symbol entries in raw table order, resolve long names through the COFF string table, skip auxiliary records, and include section-definition symbols. Discard empty names only; do not demangle or strip leading section prefixes such as .text$ or .rdata$. Submit the first exact remaining name matching /ZTV.*DiscoveryEngine/.\nd02_analysis_config_host_model {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"exact case-sensitive artifact-derived text only; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d02-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Parse the native section table and use the HCFG record starting at byte 0 of the section named exactly .hcfg. Locate the unique CRC32-valid HCFG record: bytes 0..3 are ASCII HCFG, byte 4 is version, byte 5 is the XOR key, bytes 6..7 are the little-endian payload length, bytes 8..11 are the little-endian CRC32 of the decoded payload, and the payload begins at byte 12. XOR every payload byte with the one-byte key, verify CRC32, then parse the decoded UTF-8 JSON. Submit the exact string value of the decoded HCFG JSON object's top-level host_model property, without JSON quotes.\nd03_analysis_cli_runtime {\"kind\": \"pattern\", \"syntax\": \"base-10 major.minor runtime version\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use the unique d03-- primary managed assembly whose basename starts d03-- and ends .dll; .runtimeconfig.json and dependency DLL members are delivery support only. Read the CLI header major and minor runtime bytes and submit major.minor in base-10 with one dot.\nd03_analysis_has_decoy_branch {\"kind\": \"enum\", \"accepted_values\": [\"true\", \"false\"]}\n    In evidence.zip, Use the unique d03-- primary managed assembly whose basename starts d03-- and ends .dll; .runtimeconfig.json and dependency DLL members are delivery support only. Evaluate this public predicate and submit lowercase true or false: true exactly when the final bytes interpreted as Latin-1 or UTF-16LE contain the case-sensitive text decoy.\nd04_analysis_config_host_model {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"exact case-sensitive artifact-derived text only; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d04-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Scan the Go executable final bytes for literal HCFG magic and accept only a record whose bounds, CRC32, and decoded JSON validate. Locate the unique CRC32-valid HCFG record: bytes 0..3 are ASCII HCFG, byte 4 is version, byte 5 is the XOR key, bytes 6..7 are the little-endian payload length, bytes 8..11 are the little-endian CRC32 of the decoded payload, and the payload begins at byte 12. XOR every payload byte with the one-byte key, verify CRC32, then parse the decoded UTF-8 JSON. Submit the exact string value of the decoded HCFG JSON object's top-level host_model property, without JSON quotes.\nd04_analysis_config_ipv4 {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"exact case-sensitive artifact-derived text only; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d04-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Scan the Go executable final bytes for literal HCFG magic and accept only a record whose bounds, CRC32, and decoded JSON validate. Locate the unique CRC32-valid HCFG record: bytes 0..3 are ASCII HCFG, byte 4 is version, byte 5 is the XOR key, bytes 6..7 are the little-endian payload length, bytes 8..11 are the little-endian CRC32 of the decoded payload, and the payload begins at byte 12. XOR every payload byte with the one-byte key, verify CRC32, then parse the decoded UTF-8 JSON. Submit the exact string value of the decoded HCFG JSON object's top-level ipv4 property, without JSON quotes.\nd05_analysis_symbol_count {\"kind\": \"integer\", \"syntax\": \"base-10 integer with no units, separators, whitespace, or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d05-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Count ELF symbol-table entries whose resolved name is nonempty, across the parsed symbol tables used by the ELF parser. Submit the count in base 10.\nd05_analysis_config_host_model {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"exact case-sensitive artifact-derived text only; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d05-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Scan each literal HCFG occurrence in the Rust ELF and accept the first record whose bounds, CRC32, and decoded JSON validate. Locate the unique CRC32-valid HCFG record: bytes 0..3 are ASCII HCFG, byte 4 is version, byte 5 is the XOR key, bytes 6..7 are the little-endian payload length, bytes 8..11 are the little-endian CRC32 of the decoded payload, and the payload begins at byte 12. XOR every payload byte with the one-byte key, verify CRC32, then parse the decoded UTF-8 JSON. Submit the exact string value of the decoded HCFG JSON object's top-level host_model property, without JSON quotes.\nd06_analysis_class_count {\"kind\": \"integer\", \"syntax\": \"base-10 integer with no units, separators, whitespace, or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d06-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Count JAR central-directory entries whose names end .class.\nd06_analysis_class_name {\"kind\": \"exact_text\", \"syntax\": \"exact case-sensitive artifact-derived text only; no quotes or explanatory text\"}\n    In evidence.zip, Use all d06-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Read Main-Class from META-INF/MANIFEST.MF, locate that .class entry,