{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jx2dmMoV2fi6Y232eyPRoj","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version \n\n{\"id\": \"stripped-twin-function-matching\", \"concept\": \"Match functions between two STRIPPED native builds to find the patched one (no symbols): BinDiff/Diaphora-style heuristics\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 shipped a stripped/symbolized pair; a stripped vulnerable/corrected pair is a natural escalation. Recover function starts (prologues, call targets, .eh_frame FDEs -- pyelftools CFI gives exact ranges even when stripped), then match by: referenced strings/imports, callee/caller sets, size, BB count, normalised-instruction hash, constant set; unmatched or hash-different = changed. Report the changed function's file offset/VA, its .eh_frame range and, if the symbolized twin exists in another group/member, its name. Fixtures: gcc pairs `strip -s`, -O2. 1st attempt killed rc -9 with nothing written: keep it to .eh_frame FDE ranges + normalised-instruction hashes wit\n\n{\"id\": \"multi-role-member-router\", \"concept\": \"Groups of 3+ members with roles (loader + several plugins/libraries, stub + payload, client + server), HCFG in one member only, decoy HCFG in another; ids qualified by role or unqualified with the member named in the question text\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 needed a hand-written _named_member() for unqualified ids whose question says 'Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config' and it had to run AFTER the qualifier peel. Generalize into lib.binary.route_member(group, field, question) -> (member, residual_field): qualifier peel by longest file-name token, then question phrases ('basename ends X', 'Use the dNN-- X member', 'the member that exports Y', 'the library named by the loader's DT_NEEDED', 'the member loaded by ...'), then structural fallbacks (the only member with a crc-valid HCFG\n\n{\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"V, Odin, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka, Erlang, Julia, Zig-cc/Nim-js... (Ada D17, Fortran D18, COBOL D19, Haskell D20, OCaml D21 seen)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada/Fortran/COBOL/Haskell/OCaml all landed as plain x86-64 ELFs (format elf) -- the law held; D19-D20 moved the HCFG into an overlay, D21 into a separate plugin member. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"}\n\n[]\n'},\\n  {\"i'\n'ing the literal closures (unicorn) or by hcfg_scan over the closure immediates. Fixtures: garble needs a Go toolchain (`go install mvdan.cc/garble@latest`); if Go is absent, record as a tool gap.\"}\\n]\\n```\\n'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ssdeep'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tlsh'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ppdeep'\n/usr/bin/yara","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"193ee463-6801-44d4-8936-29e540c94a22","uuid":"e77e65e8-756c-4428-b7d6-a5f701e209a8","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:53:24.881Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version \n\n{\"id\": \"stripped-twin-function-matching\", \"concept\": \"Match functions between two STRIPPED native builds to find the patched one (no symbols): BinDiff/Diaphora-style heuristics\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 shipped a stripped/symbolized pair; a stripped vulnerable/corrected pair is a natural escalation. Recover function starts (prologues, call targets, .eh_frame FDEs -- pyelftools CFI gives exact ranges even when stripped), then match by: referenced strings/imports, callee/caller sets, size, BB count, normalised-instruction hash, constant set; unmatched or hash-different = changed. Report the changed function's file offset/VA, its .eh_frame range and, if the symbolized twin exists in another group/member, its name. Fixtures: gc