ignment from them\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 'Cluster them by behavior, watch out for false friends, and sort the family from the strangers' shipped false-friend/family-a/family-b Odin ELFs (same size + 28-entry section table; a vs b = 1 differing byte, the role string in .rodata; false friend ~2k bytes from .text on, own HCFG). Only routing was asked; a D29 sequel will likely ask metrics. Build lib.binary.member_similarity(members) -> {pair: {diff_bytes, first_diff, same_sections:[...], text_sha256_equal, func_hash_overlap, string_jaccard}} + cluster_members(members, rule) where the rule is parsed from the question (equal .text hash / same HCFG JSON / same trace profile / threshold). Functions on stripped ELFs from .eh_frame FDE pc ranges (pyelftools CFI), hash = sha256 of capstone mnemonics+operand kinds (mask imm/disp/rip-rel). Fixtures: the D28 trio from challenges/day28 cases + gcc -O0/-O2 builds of one source and one different source. Expose results via register_generic for ids like `<a>_<b>_diff_bytes`, `family_members`, `false_friend`, `cluster_count`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"behavior-profile-from-trace-templates\",\"concept\":\"Behaviour vector per member from the embedded `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` records (branch, event_count, campaign, family, effects, cluster_marker_positive) and clustering by equal profiles\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Every member since D2 embeds trace JSON records; D28 members carry 4 each (failure/1, success/57, decoy/40, failure/35 for the family; the false friend 12/10/8 with the same family name `odin_family_cluster_trace`, effects `behavior_cluster_only`, `cluster_marker_positive:true`). Build lib.binary.trace_records(blob) (regex over Latin-1 + UTF-16LE + inside jar entries/.NET #US heap, json.loads each, keep order) and behavior_profile(blob) -> tuple of (branch, event_count) in file order; answer ids like `<role>_event_count`, `<role>_success_event_count`, `behavior_cluster`, `same_behavior_as_<role>`, `trace_family`, `trace_effects`, `cluster_marker_positive` for any group. Fixture: all 28 groups of the D28 single case (record count per group as a regression).\"},\n {\"id\":\"false-friend-discriminator\",\"concept\":\"Pick the odd one out among N look-alike members: which member is the false friend / stranger, how many belong to the family, the family member list -- by the metric the question names (config equality, campaign prefix, .text hash, behaviour profile, code overlap)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 named the roles in the basenames (`-false-friend`), so the routing was free; a harder variant names members neutrally (`sample-1..5.elf`, `specimen-a..e`) and asks `false_friend_member`/`stranger_members` (JSON list in CD order or sorted), `family_size`, `family_config_campaign`. Implement lib.binary.partition_family(members, question): compute HCFG JSON per member, .text sha256, behaviour profile and pairwise similarity; group by the stated equivalence; family = the largest class (ties -> raise, report); output basenames exactly as in the CD. Fixtures: shuffled/renamed copies of the D28 trio plus a 5-member set with 2 strangers.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fuzzy-hash-fields\",\"concept\":\"Fuzzy / structural hashes as answer fields: ssdeep (CTPH), TLSH, imphash (PE), telfhash/ELF import hash, Rich-header hash, md5/sha1 of sections\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Family attribution questions classically ask ssdeep/TLSH/imphash. venv has NO ssdeep/tlsh/ppdeep modules: implement pure-Python ssdeep (spamsum: rolling hash window 7, FNV-1 32-bit, base64 alphabet, block size doubling from 3; output `<bs>:<h1>:<h2>`) and ssdeep compare (edit distance score 0-100), TLSH (T1 hash, 128 buckets, Pearson, quartiles, 70-hex `T1...`) validated against the reference algorithm description; imphash via pefile.get_imphash(); telfhash = TLSH over sorted lowercased imported symbol names (excluding the documented exclusion list). Expose via register_generic for `ssdeep`, `tlsh`, `imphash`, `telfhash`, `<a>_<b>_ssdeep_score`. Fixtures: pinned outputs for a few corpus members computed once with pip ssdeep/py-tlsh in a throwaway venv if network allows, otherwise self-consistency tests + the published spamsum test vectors.\"},\n {\"id\":\"yara-rule-match-facts\",\"concept\":\"Family signature questions: evaluate a YARA rule (given in the question or derived from shared strings) against every member; count/list matches; the shared-string set that separates the family from the stranger\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"yara is installed (/usr/bin/yara and the venv module). Build lib.binary.yara_matches(rule_text, members) (compile in-process, timeout 2 s, no includes/externals) and shared_strings(members, min_len=6) -> strings present in every family member but not in the stranger (Latin-1 + UTF-16LE), with sha256 of the sorted LF-join for a pattern id. Question parsing: extract a rule between `rule ... { ... }` or a stated condition ('strings $a = \\\"...\\\" ... 2 of them'). Fixture: the D28 trio (rule on `huntress-role-family` must match a+b only).\"},\n {\"id\":\"backfill-spec-grammar-extensions\",\"concept\":\"Next backfill (#4, ~15/group) spec sentences on the 28 old groups: more predicates, counts and sorted-set hashes over the real format of each container\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Backfill #3 (D28) padded every group to 14 with sentences: substring predicates (Latin-1/UTF-16LE, OR symbol-name contains), regex counts over nonempty .symtab names (.dynsym only when no .symtab -- GM rejected the union), sorted LF-join sha256, colon-joined member-digest sha256, Jcc opcode byte scan over .text, CLI header Major.Minor, section_count (PE re-roll -> NumberOfSections), class_count/class_name, PK19 keys, overlay_size (day's own magic). Pre-register generic_field rules for the next likely sentences on EVERY container (ELF/PE/.NET/jar/wasm): segment/program-header count, import/NEEDED count + sorted sha256, export count, dynsym count, section-name predicates, per-section sha256/size/entropy, string count matching /re/, call/ret opcode counts, .NET TypeDef/MethodDef/AssemblyRef counts + sorted-name sha256, jar entry count/sorted-name sha256, constant-pool count, wasm import/export/function counts. Validate each against all 28 groups of the D28 single case (no GM truth: assert determinism + cross-tool agreement with readelf/pefile/javap/wasm-objdump).\"},\n {\"id\":\"theme-backfill-d18-d28-fields\",\"concept\":\"THEME facts of D18-D28 asked as fields on their own old groups (capstone / backfill #4): d18 call graph, d19/d20 overlay headers, d21 NEEDED/exports/handshake, d22 ImplMap rows, d23 predicates, d24/d25 changed method + bug class, d26 call chain/throw site, d27 per-role toolchain, d28 cluster membership\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Backfill #3 already reached into themes (d19 packing_key_1/2_hex, d20 overlay_size, d23/d03 has_decoy_branch, d26 method_names_sha256, d18 handler_symbols_sha256). Build one facts dict per themed group from the bytes: d18 callees per subprogram; d19 PK19 ver/len/sha256/unpacked size; d20 RS20 ver/res_len/scratch_len/scratch_sha256; d21 loader NEEDED list, plugin exports, `caml_plugin_header`; d22 ImplMap (import name, ModuleRef, callconv); d23 TypeRef/MemberRef predicate APIs + compared env values; d24 changed method name/descriptor (`score(Ljava/lang/String;)I`), d25 `parse_frame` + guard constant 4; d26 stageOne->stageTwo->stageThree + thrown class; d27 per-role debug format (dwarf/stabs), producer, symbol count, hash style; d28 family/false-friend roles, diff bytes, campaign prefixes. Register as generic_field rules keyed by field name + question sentence; tests over the D28 single case artifacts.\"},\n {\"id\":\"toolchain-attribution-verdicts\",\"concept\":\"Toolchain attribution as enum/text answers per member: compiler (gcc/clang/tcc/zig/msvc/mingw/odin/v), compiler version, linker (bfd/gold/lld/mold/tcc/link.exe), libc (glibc/musl/bionic/msvcrt/ucrt), debug format (dwarf2-5/stabs/codeview/none), static vs dynamic, PIE, hash style\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 'name the toolchain' was unasked and D28 moved on to family clustering, but a D29 lineage/attribution step or the D31 capstone could ask it on d27/d28. Evidence rules: .comment banner (often stripped), DW_AT_producer (`readelf --debug-dump=info`), .stab/.stabstr (tcc), `.lto_priv`/`.constprop` (gcc LTO), `.note.gnu.gold-version` (gold), `.comment` `Linker: LLD` (lld), `mold` in .comment, tcc unmerged `.text.<fn>` + per-object GNU_PROPERTY notes, PE Rich header comp ids (MSVC) vs MinGW `.CRT`/`__mingw_` symbols, PT_INTERP (ld-musl vs ld-linux), Odin `/odin/base/runtime` paths, V `builtin__`/`_vinit`. Output tokens lowercase; when an enum is supplied pick from it. Fixtures: gcc/clang-18/tcc(if apt)/aarch64-gcc builds of one C file with -g/-s variants + the d27/d28 members.\"},\n {\"id\":\"odin-language-facts\",\"concept\":\"Odin binary identity + facts (D28 language) for a d28 backfill: has_odin_runtime predicate, runtime source paths, package/procedure symbol names when unstripped, Odin-specific sections/strings, role string\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 members: ELF64 PIE, glibc dynamic (NEEDED libm.so.6, libc.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2), stripped (~20 .dynsym entries: __libc_start_main@GLIBC_2.34 etc.), strings `/odin/base/runtime/os_specific_linux.odin`, `/odin/base/runtime/default_temp_allocator_arena.odin`, `base/runtime: getrandom not available in kernel`, role string `huntress-role-<role>`, HCFG RAW appended at e_shoff+e_shnum*64, 4 trace records. Unstripped Odin symbols look like `<package>.<proc>` / `runtime.` / `__$startup_runtime`. Add these to language_of() and register generic predicates (`has_odin_runtime`: final bytes contain `/odin/` or `base/runtime`; `odin_runtime_path_count`). Odin compiler is not installed (no fixtures beyond the D28 members) -- use the challenges/day28 cases.\"},\n {\"id\":\"hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"Next niche native languages as a new-day member (D29-D31): Hare (QBE backend, static, no libc, `rt.`/`hare.` symbols), C3 (`c3`-mangled `module.func`), Vala/Genie (GObject C: `g_object_new`, `_vala_`/`*_get_type`, NEEDED libglib/libgobject), Cython (`__pyx_` .so), hxcpp (`hx::`), Jakt/Carbon-style transpilers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The language track since D27 picks niche native languages the atlas listed (V, Odin). Prebuild cue strings + language_of() entries and make sure header ids + HCFG scan (raw, base64, appended tail) work on each: Vala/Genie can be built locally if `valac` is apt-installable (`apt-get install valac`), Cython with the venv (`pip download` not needed: write C by hand mimicking `__pyx_` symbols if offline); Hare/C3 likely not installable -> synthesise minimal static ELFs with gcc -nostdlib exposing their symbol shapes (`rt.start_ha`, `hare.main`, `.test_array`) and an appended HCFG to test routing. Record install status per toolchain in detail on failure.\"},\n]\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\nassert not ids & {x['id'] for x in new}\ng=new+g\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable\nbody='\\n'+'[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x, ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]\\n'\nt=t[:s]+body+t[e:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n# validate\nt2=open(p).read(); s2=t2.index('```json',t2.index('## Readiness gaps'))+7; e2=t2.index('```',s2)\ng2=json.loads(t2[s2:e2]); print(len(g2), sum(1 for x in g2 if x['priority']==1), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g2))\nprint([x['id'] for x in g2 if x['priority']==1])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":180869,"cache_creation":{