riend roles, diff bytes, campaign prefixes. Register as generic_field rules keyed by field name + question sentence; tests over the D28 single case artifacts.\"},\n {\"id\":\"toolchain-attribution-verdicts\",\"concept\":\"Toolchain attribution as enum/text answers per member: compiler (gcc/clang/tcc/zig/msvc/mingw/odin/v), compiler version, linker (bfd/gold/lld/mold/tcc/link.exe), libc (glibc/musl/bionic/msvcrt/ucrt), debug format (dwarf2-5/stabs/codeview/none), static vs dynamic, PIE, hash style\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 'name the toolchain' was unasked and D28 moved on to family clustering, but a D29 lineage/attribution step or the D31 capstone could ask it on d27/d28. Evidence rules: .comment banner (often stripped), DW_AT_producer (`readelf --debug-dump=info`), .stab/.stabstr (tcc), `.lto_priv`/`.constprop` (gcc LTO), `.note.gnu.gold-version` (gold), `.comment` `Linker: LLD` (lld), `mold` in .comment, tcc unmerged `.text.<fn>` + per-object GNU_PROPERTY notes, PE Rich header comp ids (MSVC) vs MinGW `.CRT`/`__mingw_` symbols, PT_INTERP (ld-musl vs ld-linux), Odin `/odin/base/runtime` paths, V `builtin__`/`_vinit`. Output tokens lowercase; when an enum is supplied pick from it. Fixtures: gcc/clang-18/tcc(if apt)/aarch64-gcc builds of one C file with -g/-s variants + the d27/d28 members.\"},\n {\"id\":\"odin-language-facts\",\"concept\":\"Odin binary identity + facts (D28 language) for a d28 backfill: has_odin_runtime predicate, runtime source paths, package/procedure symbol names when unstripped, Odin-specific sections/strings, role string\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 members: ELF64 PIE, glibc dynamic (NEEDED libm.so.6, libc.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2), stripped (~20 .dynsym entries: __libc_start_main@GLIBC_2.34 etc.), strings `/odin/base/runtime/os_specific_linux.odin`, `/odin/base/runtime/default_temp_allocator_arena.odin`, `base/runtime: getrandom not available in kernel`, role string `huntress-role-<role>`, HCFG RAW appended at e_shoff+e_shnum*64, 4 trace records. Unstripped Odin symbols look like `<package>.<proc>` / `runtime.` / `__$startup_runtime`. Add these to language_of() and register generic predicates (`has_odin_runtime`: final bytes contain `/odin/` or `base/runtime`; `odin_runtime_path_count`). Odin compiler is not installed (no fixtures beyond the D28 members) -- use the challenges/day28 cases.\"},\n {\"id\":\"hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"Next niche native languages as a new-day member (D29-D31): Hare (QBE backend, static, no libc, `rt.`/`hare.` symbols), C3 (`c3`-mangled `module.func`), Vala/Genie (GObject C: `g_object_new`, `_vala_`/`*_get_type`, NEEDED libglib/libgobject), Cython (`__pyx_` .so), hxcpp (`hx::`), Jakt/Carbon-style transpilers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The language track since D27 picks niche native languages the atlas listed (V, Odin). Prebuild cue strings + language_of() entries and make sure header ids + HCFG scan (raw, base64, appended tail) work on each: Vala/Genie can be built locally if `valac` is apt-installable (`apt-get install valac`), Cython with the venv (`pip download` not needed: write C by hand mimicking `__pyx_` symbols if offline); Hare/C3 likely not installable -> synthesise minimal static ELFs with gcc -nostdlib exposing their symbol shapes (`rt.start_ha`, `hare.main`, `.test_array`) and an appended HCFG to test routing. Record install status per toolchain in detail on failure.\"},\n]\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\nassert not ids & {x['id'] for x in new}\ng=new+g\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable\nbody='\\n'+'[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x, ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]\\n'\nt=t[:s]+body+t[e:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n# validate\nt2=open(p).read(); s2=t2.index('```json',t2.index('## Readiness gaps'))+7; e2=t2.index('```',s2)\ng2=json.loads(t2[s2:e2]); print(len(g2), sum(1 for x in g2 if x['priority']==1), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g2))\nprint([x['id'] for x in g2 if x['priority']==1])\nEOF"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01HY5CRKnXLEqx5iZcP2pUVY":{"cwd":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026"}}}
